.TH GITHUB-COPILOT-INSTALLER 1 "September 2026" "github-copilot-installer 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
github-copilot-installer \- install GitHub's official GitHub Copilot RPM on Fedora
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B github-copilot-installer
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B github-copilot-installer
retrieves release metadata from GitHub, downloads the official GitHub Copilot
RPM, verifies its published SHA-256 digest and package identity, and delegates
installation or updates to DNF.
.PP
The GitHub Copilot application is proprietary and is not contained in the
installer package or its COPR repository.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Install the latest selected GitHub Copilot release.
.TP
.B update
Update an existing recognized GitHub Copilot installation.
.TP
.B status
Show the helper and installed application versions, without network access
or temporary files.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the upstream application package while retaining user data.
.TP
.B version
Print the helper version.
.TP
.B help
Print command usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-version " VERSION"
Select an explicit GitHub Copilot release instead of the latest release.
Valid only with install and update.
.TP
.BR \-\-assumeyes ", " \-y
Pass automatic yes confirmation to DNF. Valid only for mutating commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.copilot
Upstream application data. This helper never removes or modifies it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo github-copilot-installer install
github-copilot-installer status
sudo github-copilot-installer update --assumeyes
sudo github-copilot-installer uninstall
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The upstream RPM is unsigned. Installation therefore requires the SHA-256
digest published by the official GitHub release API and an exact official
release URL.
